# Publishable (anon) key — safe in a client; RLS + require_admin() are the real gate.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://izlyevebmxqlxinigote.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_Ve9ENI8gAovucWDHRzKuRg_TaVW_Uhe

# Service role key. SERVER ONLY — never prefix this NEXT_PUBLIC_, never import
# it into a client component, and never commit a real value here.
#
# It bypasses RLS and every private.require_admin() guard in the database. It
# exists for exactly one thing: creating an owner's auth account, because
# profiles.id is a foreign key to auth.users(id) and no RPC can mint one. See
# lib/supabase/admin.ts.
#
# Leave it unset and the console still works — the add-salon flow just cannot
# create a brand-new owner, only attach a salon to an existing account.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Outbound email, for the app-waitlist launch announcement. SERVER ONLY.
#
# Leave these unset and the send path still works end to end — every recipient
# is claimed, attempted and recorded — but nothing leaves the server and the
# send dialog says so on screen. That is the same simulate-when-unconfigured
# seam tho's notification worker uses for push and SMS, and it is what lets the
# whole queue be exercised before anyone buys an email plan.
#
# EMAIL_API_URL defaults to Resend. Any provider that takes a JSON POST of
# {from, to[], subject, html, text} with a bearer token works by changing the
# URL alone.
EMAIL_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=
# EMAIL_API_URL=https://api.resend.com/emails
